  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nHigh pressure with dry conditions will exit the area this evening,\ngiving way to showers and thunderstorms this weekend. Some slow \nmoving storms and heavy rain are expected at times. Isolated strong \nstorms are possible on Saturday. Ahead of the upper level trough\nsparking this rainfall, a surface low will move northeast and park\nover Lake Erie overnight Sunday. The upper and surface low will get\nhung up over West Virginia early Monday, with some lingering light \nshowers possible over and east of the Scioto River Valley.\n\nThe upper low is expected to retrograde and park itself over the CWA\nTuesday morning and then finally exit Wednesday night. Off and on\nlight showers are possible through this period as the low remains\noverhead. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nWarmer temps are expected today, generally in the mid 80s. With \nthe expected cloud cover and rain over the weekend, highs will be\nlimited to the 70s and low 80s. A gradual warming trend will occur \nfor the coming week with highs in the middle to upper 80s by mid-\nweek.",
